flowchart TB
  accTitle: Website account handover to DorkOS Cloud
  accDescr: Without a valid configured accounts origin the website serves local accounts. When configured, selected browser routes redirect and machine calls proxy to the accounts origin. Managed connections need an independent forwarding switch and service availability; their migration evidence stays separate. This diagram describes code behavior, not the production switch state.

  browser["<b>Browser</b><br/><span class='d'>Account pages and navigation</span>"]
  machine["<b>App or machine</b><br/><span class='d'>Account and instance calls</span>"]
  site["<b>Website forwarding policy</b><br/><span class='d'>Per route, when an accounts origin is configured</span>"]
  local["<b>Website account pages</b><br/><span class='d'>Serve locally while no origin is set</span>"]
  accounts["<b>Cloud account origin</b><br/><span class='d'>A separate hosted sign-in surface</span>"]
  managed["<b>Managed connections</b><br/><span class='d'>Need a second switch · unavailable until then</span>"]
  public["<b>Public website</b><br/><span class='d'>Docs · marketing · marketplace · stays local</span>"]

  browser --> site
  machine --> site
  site -->|"no origin, or invalid"| local
  site -->|"307 redirect<br/><span class='d'>account pages, eligible navigation</span>"| accounts
  site -->|"proxy<br/><span class='d'>bearer, body and background calls · query kept</span>"| accounts
  site -->|"second switch off"| managed
  site -->|"second switch on<br/><span class='d'>service first, cron ownership follows</span>"| accounts
  site -->|"public routes"| public

  classDef cloud fill:#fff5e4,stroke:#a87720,color:#49320c
  classDef external fill:#ffffff,stroke:#8a9bab,color:#3b4a58
  class accounts cloud
  class browser external
